WEBVTT

01:32.400 --> 01:34.610
<i>Christmas Eve.</i>

01:35.440 --> 01:39.410
<i>The city is awash in jingle bells
and Christmas lighting,</i>

01:39.410 --> 01:44.870
<i>and those in love
slowly give in to the romantic night.</i>

01:55.510 --> 01:56.380
<i>However...</i>

02:01.760 --> 02:03.640
First, let me ask you.

02:03.970 --> 02:05.140
What's this?

02:05.770 --> 02:07.390
A Christmas pine!

02:07.940 --> 02:09.020
And this?

02:09.020 --> 02:10.650
A lion dance reindeer.

02:10.980 --> 02:12.650
Who are you?

02:14.190 --> 02:15.900
I'm Demon Santa!

02:16.990 --> 02:19.860
Why does your family mash up
Christmas and New Year's?

02:21.490 --> 02:23.950
I totally hear you, President.

02:23.950 --> 02:26.290
We felt the same way at first.

02:26.660 --> 02:30.670
A few years ago, we left the tree out
long after Christmas ended,

02:30.670 --> 02:32.790
and my sister turned it
into a New Year's pine!

02:34.000 --> 02:37.800
We went on using it every year
so as not to be wasteful...

02:39.470 --> 02:44.310
until we came to believe that this was
precisely what Christmas should look like.

02:44.310 --> 02:46.890
Don't spread your own self-serving culture!

02:46.890 --> 02:47.680
<i>Oh, crap!</i>

02:47.930 --> 02:49.810
<i>I was planning to make this
a glamorous night</i>

02:49.810 --> 02:52.940
<i>and clear the air with Shinomiya
about where we stand!</i>

02:54.320 --> 02:55.020
I'm repulsing the wishful thinkers!
This house is clean!

02:55.020 --> 02:57.820
<i>What is this eccentric pagan festival?</i>
I'm repulsing the wishful thinkers!
This house is clean!

02:58.190 --> 03:01.110
Asking Fujiwara to take care
of the preparations was a mistake.

03:01.110 --> 03:03.320
Oh, let it go, Miyuki.

03:03.320 --> 03:06.740
I mean, ringing in the New Year
and chilling with everyone...

03:07.080 --> 03:08.200
is not half bad.

03:08.540 --> 03:11.000
What did I tell you?
Now even you're in New Year's mode, Kei!

03:11.000 --> 03:12.420
Sleepy...
What did I tell you?
Now even you're in New Year's mode, Kei!

03:12.750 --> 03:16.340
I'm quite thrilled
to spend New Year's with you all.

03:16.340 --> 03:19.220
Well, if you're okay with it, Shinomiya.

03:19.510 --> 03:21.720
I brought everyone some soft drinks!

03:22.050 --> 03:23.340
All right, everybody!

03:26.760 --> 03:29.230
Merry Christmas!

03:30.600 --> 03:31.980
Now then, you guys...

03:32.310 --> 03:34.270
Cheers!

03:39.740 --> 03:42.240
Cheers!

04:15.520 --> 04:16.480
All righty!

04:16.480 --> 04:19.320
The moment you've all been waiting for!
Gift exchange time!

04:20.650 --> 04:23.570
We're going to draw lots
to decide which gifts we get!

04:23.820 --> 04:24.950
Oh...

04:24.950 --> 04:27.950
So, we'll be drawing chopsticks?
Let me see those—

04:29.660 --> 04:33.750
If you touch these chopsticks
with your candle-wax-covered hands,

04:33.750 --> 04:36.170
it'll corrupt the lots!

04:36.170 --> 04:37.590
Okay, I'm gonna draw one!

04:38.500 --> 04:39.340
Ta-da!

04:39.340 --> 04:41.090
Hey! That's mine!

04:41.670 --> 04:42.970
My gift is...

04:43.590 --> 04:44.470
a picture book.

04:44.470 --> 04:45.840
So cute!

04:46.140 --> 04:50.850
Humph!

04:51.720 --> 04:52.730
<i>A book!</i>

04:53.060 --> 04:54.640
<i>I could've run with that!</i>

04:54.640 --> 04:58.230
<i>Between Kaguya's erratic behavior
and his own hospitalization...</i>

04:58.560 --> 05:03.030
<i>Shirogane could only manage
some last-minute gift-shopping.</i>

05:03.360 --> 05:06.990
<i>What could I give
someone as rich as Shinomiya?</i>

05:06.990 --> 05:09.620
<i>After much agonizing,
what he picked out was...</i>

05:10.910 --> 05:12.540
<i>a handkerchief.</i>

05:12.540 --> 05:15.500
<i>A present that shoots far past the comfort zone
and couldn't be less exciting.</i>

05:15.960 --> 05:17.040
<i>This is a devastating failure
on Shirogane's part!</i>

05:17.040 --> 05:19.290
Now it's your turn, Kei!
<i>This is a devastating failure
on Shirogane's part!</i>

05:19.290 --> 05:20.250
<i>Come on!</i>

05:20.250 --> 05:23.380
<i>Just let everyone else's gifts
be as boring as possible!</i>

05:23.380 --> 05:25.510
Huh? Did I just draw yours, Kaguya?

05:26.550 --> 05:28.970
There's an aroma diffuser inside.

05:29.430 --> 05:31.970
I've also included some essential oils.

05:33.390 --> 05:35.140
I'll use them with care!

05:35.140 --> 05:37.390
Please share them with your brother.

05:38.520 --> 05:40.360
<i>Nice going, Shinomiya!</i>

05:40.360 --> 05:42.530
<i>You sure come up with the best gifts!</i>

05:42.820 --> 05:43.530
<i>But...</i>

05:43.860 --> 05:46.400
<i>look whose are left!
The Fujiwara Sisters who decorated this house!</i>

05:46.820 --> 05:52.160
<i>I just know they got presents so eye-popping
they'll blast my boring gift into oblivion!</i>

05:53.910 --> 05:55.200
I shall pick...

05:56.960 --> 05:58.080
Miss Chika...

05:58.080 --> 05:59.540
Fujiwara's gift, right?

06:01.540 --> 06:03.170
My present is...

06:03.670 --> 06:05.920
homemade bath bombs!

06:06.220 --> 06:07.260
Bath bombs?

06:07.260 --> 06:11.300
Yes! You put them in the bathtub,
and they fizzle and smell great! It's fun!

06:11.300 --> 06:13.680
<i>Can't you be more blunt?</i>

06:13.680 --> 06:17.180
<i>You're the type who can make people
squirm with your retorts!</i>

06:18.560 --> 06:19.900
<i>My last hope is...</i>

06:20.480 --> 06:21.150
Hey!

06:21.770 --> 06:25.030
That means you and I
will be exchanging gifts, President!

06:25.030 --> 06:26.280
What a coincidence!

06:26.780 --> 06:29.660
- You rigged it that way, didn't you?
- President Shirogane's present is...

06:30.610 --> 06:31.620
a handkerchief!

06:32.240 --> 06:34.160
How simple and nice!

06:34.160 --> 06:37.910
More like simple and... boring, huh?

06:38.960 --> 06:41.250
Please open mine now!

06:42.670 --> 06:43.590
<i>I'm begging you!</i>

06:43.960 --> 06:45.500
<i>Let it be something weird!</i>

06:50.340 --> 06:53.600
Moeha! What kind of gift
is that to give to my brother?

06:54.140 --> 06:55.560
I'm sorry, President!

06:55.560 --> 06:58.850
I'm the only normal person in my family!
Everyone else is an oddball!

06:59.480 --> 07:00.850
No.

07:01.560 --> 07:03.310
I'm so thrilled.

07:03.310 --> 07:04.900
Whaaaaat?

07:04.900 --> 07:07.860
Thank you, Fujiwara's little sister.
This is exactly what I've been wanting.

07:08.240 --> 07:11.360
Moeha! You spiked my brother's drink
with something, didn't you?

07:11.360 --> 07:15.280
If you're not sure how to use them,
ask me anytime!

07:15.280 --> 07:19.370
What do you mean, "how to use them"?
What do you mean? Whaaaaat?

07:36.850 --> 07:38.310
Presents...

07:40.020 --> 07:42.310
We didn't draw each other's, did we?

07:43.020 --> 07:44.270
I guess not.

07:45.060 --> 07:46.020
President...

07:48.070 --> 07:51.070
Don't let the others find out about this.

07:53.410 --> 07:55.410
Please open it when you get home.

07:55.410 --> 07:57.540
Th-Thanks.

08:00.250 --> 08:01.750
Don't you...

08:02.160 --> 08:03.290
have one for me?

08:03.920 --> 08:05.130
Something...

08:05.460 --> 08:06.540
for me...

08:07.550 --> 08:08.340
I do.

08:17.010 --> 08:17.930
No.

08:18.680 --> 08:19.890
Sorry, I can't!

08:19.890 --> 08:22.060
Because this is something random
that I picked up!

08:22.430 --> 08:24.560
It's fine. I don't mind
if it was random.

08:24.560 --> 08:25.440
I can't!

08:26.440 --> 08:29.320
No, really, I was so slammed when I chose it!

08:29.320 --> 08:32.190
And now I have no idea
why I'd buy anything like this!

08:32.740 --> 08:35.700
This isn't for you!
I wanna give you something more perfect—

08:38.700 --> 08:40.540
You really have no clue!

08:40.540 --> 08:43.460
I'm telling you
it doesn't have to be perfect!

08:52.970 --> 08:55.220
I'm telling you
it doesn't have to be perfect!

08:56.840 --> 09:00.560
If this present is an aspect of yourself
that you don't wish me to see,

09:00.560 --> 09:02.600
then I'm never going to let go!

09:02.600 --> 09:04.350
I don't know what you mean by that!

09:07.770 --> 09:10.230
Fujiwara, you talk some sense into her!

09:10.570 --> 09:11.730
Miss Fujiwara?

09:18.240 --> 09:19.620
<i>I should've known!</i>

09:28.670 --> 09:32.000
<i>That present is a part of President
that he wants to hide.</i>

09:32.710 --> 09:34.470
<i>He's always like this!</i>

09:34.470 --> 09:37.680
<i>Trying so hard, overdoing it
to a worrying degree!</i>

09:37.680 --> 09:41.510
<i>Taking so much time and care
to show me something perfect!</i>

09:44.560 --> 09:47.770
<i>But I also wanna know
the you who's not like that!</i>

09:47.770 --> 09:49.810
<i>I want to see you! To unmask you!</i>

09:50.810 --> 09:53.280
Truly, you're so stubborn!

09:53.730 --> 09:56.530
President, you said
you purchased that for me!

09:56.860 --> 09:59.160
So, it belongs to me now!

09:59.160 --> 10:02.280
I said I can't give it to you!
How selfish are you anyway, Shinomiya?

10:03.990 --> 10:05.290
I knew it.

10:07.460 --> 10:11.590
The truth is, you hate me,
and that's why you won't show it to me!

10:11.590 --> 10:12.210
Huh?

10:12.590 --> 10:14.550
You might as well say it directly!

10:14.550 --> 10:17.050
That you hate harsh women
with horrible personalities like me!

10:17.510 --> 10:19.550
That's why you won't show it to me, right?

10:20.140 --> 10:23.890
I showed you my true self,
because I wanted you to show me your true self!

10:23.890 --> 10:25.180
What are you talking about?

10:25.520 --> 10:26.930
What other reason can there be?

10:26.930 --> 10:29.940
Doesn't everybody want the person they love
to see their true self?

10:30.440 --> 10:31.940
The person they love?

10:31.940 --> 10:34.440
I don't want to keep secrets
from the person I love!

10:37.490 --> 10:41.320
To be able to share everything,
to understand each other completely!

10:41.320 --> 10:43.950
What could be lovelier than that?

10:44.740 --> 10:48.250
I've been trying to be more likable lately.

10:48.250 --> 10:51.710
But scratch the surface,
and this is who I am.

10:52.000 --> 10:56.800
I was sure that if I continued to hide
the selfish, disagreeable and aggressive me,

10:56.800 --> 10:59.720
I could never advance to the next level!

11:03.760 --> 11:08.230
I showed you my weak side!
Because I want us to understand each other!

11:08.600 --> 11:09.980
That's why...

11:10.480 --> 11:14.480
now, I want you to show me
your weak side!

11:15.570 --> 11:17.740
I get what you're trying to say.

11:18.190 --> 11:21.160
And I think it'd be ideal if I could do that.

11:22.410 --> 11:24.530
But it's the opposite for me.

11:24.870 --> 11:28.750
Don't you think it's because you love someone
that you can't show them your weak side?

11:29.120 --> 11:32.290
Like, "What if I show my weak side,
and it disillusions her?"

11:32.290 --> 11:35.920
or "What if she sees something in me
that's unacceptable?"

11:36.920 --> 11:41.010
The stronger my feelings for her,
the more I can't let her see that side of me!

11:41.680 --> 11:43.010
I understand your rationale!

11:45.220 --> 11:48.970
But as I've shown you my true self,
please show me yours, President!

11:48.970 --> 11:50.520
Otherwise, I will have shown you
for nothing!

11:50.810 --> 11:52.520
You're so stubborn!

11:53.190 --> 11:55.610
You make it sound like terms for a trade!

11:55.610 --> 11:58.190
But it's not even a trade
in the first place!

11:58.610 --> 12:01.280
You say that you have
a horrible personality...

12:01.280 --> 12:06.370
but I knew that going in,
and I've never thought it was negative!

12:07.330 --> 12:08.450
At first,

12:08.740 --> 12:10.910
I thought you looked down on people

12:10.910 --> 12:13.040
and that you were keeping
your distance from others.

12:14.580 --> 12:20.300
But when it hit me that you were distancing
yourself because you didn't want to hurt anyone,

12:21.090 --> 12:23.010
I thought, "Hey, that's sweet!"

12:25.050 --> 12:28.430
From the get-go,
I liked that side of you,

12:28.430 --> 12:33.640
so telling me to show my weak side because
you showed me yours doesn't make us equal.

12:34.480 --> 12:37.480
But I can't look cool unless I try to.

12:37.770 --> 12:39.570
So I avoid doing anything
to stir up a hornet's nest—

12:39.570 --> 12:40.990
Oh, how you do go on and on!

12:41.320 --> 12:42.570
Just show it to me!

12:42.570 --> 12:43.650
Hey, come on!

12:43.650 --> 12:47.280
I assure you, no matter what kind
of present it is, it'll be fine!

12:47.280 --> 12:49.910
You may not think so, but I'm far more...

13:06.050 --> 13:06.890
You're good.

13:07.720 --> 13:09.640
Why did you give me a cup-and-ball toy?

13:10.010 --> 13:12.390
Somewhere along the way,
I lost sight, myself!

13:12.890 --> 13:14.690
I had to pick something out in a rush!

13:14.690 --> 13:17.270
But it wasn't like I could just get
something cheap and be done with it!

13:17.650 --> 13:20.860
After a lot of process of elimination,
it came down to this cup-and-ball toy.

13:23.150 --> 13:24.280
How absurd!

13:27.160 --> 13:30.280
Now I can see
why you wanted to run away!

13:30.580 --> 13:32.830
This isn't romantic in the least!

13:32.830 --> 13:34.790
Hey, you don't have to laugh so hard.

13:34.790 --> 13:36.370
You sure are cruel.

13:36.750 --> 13:38.420
However, look.

13:39.880 --> 13:42.800
Do I seem at all disillusioned?

13:50.220 --> 13:52.220
Ridiculous, isn't it?

13:52.220 --> 13:54.810
In a park like this,
devoid of Christmas lights...

13:55.390 --> 13:57.310
It wasn't supposed to be like this.

13:57.690 --> 13:59.060
This is what I want.

13:59.650 --> 14:02.320
I don't need lights or balloons.

14:03.190 --> 14:07.570
Not that those balloons
weren't lovely and romantic...

14:08.030 --> 14:11.080
but it doesn't have to be like that.

14:15.120 --> 14:17.080
Because I find ordinary things like this...

14:18.330 --> 14:21.340
to be romantic.

14:22.420 --> 14:24.590
Ordinary, huh?

14:28.010 --> 14:29.590
Tell me, President...

14:30.300 --> 14:32.850
on Christmas Eve,
what would a couple...

14:34.180 --> 14:37.850
ordinarily do at a time like this?

14:41.940 --> 14:45.860
If you're okay with ordinary.
Something like this, I guess.

15:02.420 --> 15:03.920
<i>Hey, President...</i>

15:04.840 --> 15:06.300
<i>Look at me.</i>

15:06.960 --> 15:08.720
<i>I won't hide who I am.</i>

15:09.340 --> 15:10.720
<i>Show me who you are.</i>

15:11.720 --> 15:13.220
<i>And I'll accept it.</i>

15:14.890 --> 15:20.140
<i>Some might laugh it off as sugarcoating
to want to show each other everything.</i>

15:20.480 --> 15:24.150
<i>There must be a wiser,
more graceful way to handle this.</i>

15:25.400 --> 15:27.150
<i>But in my eyes...</i>

15:27.650 --> 15:30.200
<i>this is romantic.</i>

15:31.740 --> 15:34.070
<i>Not to have anything to hide...</i>

15:34.580 --> 15:37.160
<i>is the most romantic thing...</i>

15:37.910 --> 15:39.460
<i>I can offer you.</i>

15:41.920 --> 15:46.420
<i>Our second kiss was a light one,
our lips barely brushing...</i>

15:46.800 --> 15:51.930
<i>and yet, somehow, my heart pounded
as hard as it did during the culture festival.</i>

15:52.720 --> 15:54.930
<i>Surely every time I discover
something new about you...</i>

15:56.100 --> 15:57.470
<i>it will feel like...</i>

15:57.930 --> 16:00.770
<i>I'm kissing you for the first time.</i>

16:17.660 --> 16:18.950
Finally...

16:19.620 --> 16:21.830
you're holding my hand.

16:21.830 --> 16:24.580
Though it's frozen through and cold.

16:24.960 --> 16:26.460
I don't mind.

16:33.090 --> 16:34.720
Shinomiya, do you...

16:35.300 --> 16:39.270
Do you think that I shouldn't aim
so high all the time?

16:40.020 --> 16:42.810
I must say that I don't want you
to overdo it.

16:42.810 --> 16:47.480
But if I hadn't,
we never would've ended up like this.

16:47.480 --> 16:48.860
It's all because I pushed myself.

16:48.860 --> 16:51.490
You may be right about that.

16:52.240 --> 16:54.660
But the same goes for me.

16:54.660 --> 16:58.870
If I, too, had continued
to act coldly toward you...

16:59.620 --> 17:03.370
I'm certain that somewhere along the line,
you would've deserted me.

17:03.790 --> 17:08.130
You and I both aimed high,
each taking a step toward each other...

17:08.840 --> 17:13.130
and I believe that's why
we're here now, holding hands.

17:13.470 --> 17:16.640
Then, that means we need to aim high.

17:16.640 --> 17:18.140
Perhaps.

17:18.470 --> 17:20.600
Since you're stubborn, President,

17:20.600 --> 17:24.600
I'm sure you're going to continue
to run yourself into the ground.

17:26.270 --> 17:27.270
But...

17:27.730 --> 17:31.400
when you feel exhausted,
why don't we take a little break together?

17:32.280 --> 17:34.280
Just a little at a time.

17:34.280 --> 17:36.530
From time to time,
let's drop the bravado...

17:36.990 --> 17:38.700
and lean on each other...

17:39.030 --> 17:41.040
and be there for each other
when one of us is about to collapse.

17:42.080 --> 17:46.040
Our hands may be cold,
but holding them will warm them up.

17:47.080 --> 17:51.630
Surely, isn't that what it means
to be in a relationship?

17:52.090 --> 17:55.720
Shinomiya, you're fine
with having a guy like me?

17:55.720 --> 17:58.050
No matter what an awful person
I might be?

17:58.470 --> 17:59.430
Yes.

18:14.610 --> 18:15.820
<i>Kaguya?</i>

18:16.110 --> 18:19.570
<i>Where'd you run off to?
We're gonna play a board game!</i>

18:19.570 --> 18:22.080
I'm sorry. I'll be right there.

18:24.620 --> 18:26.330
How inopportune.

18:27.160 --> 18:28.580
You said it.

18:31.170 --> 18:34.460
We won't have a white Christmas
in Tokyo this year again.

18:34.880 --> 18:36.590
That's perfectly fine.

18:37.010 --> 18:38.800
That's ordinary.

18:39.130 --> 18:42.100
Although I must say
I was taken aback by this present.

18:42.100 --> 18:44.970
Yeah, but it happens to be
a pretty swanky one!

18:44.970 --> 18:45.600
Yes.

18:46.520 --> 18:48.600
I can see that this fabric is first-class.

18:51.440 --> 18:53.650
<i>I want to have an ordinary relationship.</i>

18:55.440 --> 18:57.780
<i>I want to be an ordinary girl.</i>

18:58.150 --> 19:00.110
<i>To laugh and cry whenever I want.</i>

19:01.070 --> 19:04.620
<i>That's the kind of sweet person
I thought that I wished to be.</i>

19:05.240 --> 19:09.370
<i>I thought it would be wonderful
to be able to be kind to others.</i>

19:10.790 --> 19:12.460
<i>I want to be sweet.</i>

19:12.920 --> 19:14.380
<i>Can I become sweet?</i>

19:20.300 --> 19:23.050
<i>I want to become someone...</i>

19:23.050 --> 19:24.560
<i>who can love herself.</i>

19:30.600 --> 19:31.940
What do you think?

19:33.190 --> 19:34.190
You look cute.

19:36.230 --> 19:38.150
President said I looked cute!

19:38.490 --> 19:41.820
He did no such thing.
He definitely said that to me.

19:41.820 --> 19:43.530
But that's my ribbon!

19:44.740 --> 19:48.160
Who cares which one it was,
you're all me anyway.

19:48.160 --> 19:50.960
This should be evaluated
based on all past actions!

19:50.960 --> 19:52.960
You're trying to trick us
by using those big words!

19:52.960 --> 19:53.710
<i>Needless to say, these are all
merely images inside her mind,</i>
You're trying to trick us
by using those big words!

19:53.710 --> 19:54.960
Old trash like you can shut up!
<i>Needless to say, these are all
merely images inside her mind,</i>

19:54.960 --> 19:57.760
When you put on that ribbon,
you became me! Therefore—
<i>Needless to say, these are all
merely images inside her mind,</i>

19:57.760 --> 19:58.760
- Objection!
- Denied!
<i>Needless to say, these are all
merely images inside her mind,</i>

19:58.760 --> 19:59.510
<i>and super-deformed is just that.
Super-deformed.</i>

19:59.510 --> 20:00.930
Your Honor!
<i>and super-deformed is just that.
Super-deformed.</i>

20:00.930 --> 20:01.840
<i>and super-deformed is just that.
Super-deformed.</i>

20:01.840 --> 20:03.930
<i>That's right. This is...</i>

20:04.260 --> 20:07.930
<i>the super-deformed version
of a young girl's wavering heart.</i>

20:09.310 --> 20:10.680
President, your winter break...

20:11.060 --> 20:13.440
Would you please spare a day for me?

20:13.440 --> 20:15.440
What? Sure.

20:16.570 --> 20:18.030
Let's go on a date.

20:18.030 --> 20:20.690
There's something that I'd like
to say to you in actual words.

20:25.830 --> 20:28.200
Why do people confess their feelings?

20:28.540 --> 20:30.000
First of all,

20:30.540 --> 20:32.710
let me see your palms.

20:33.000 --> 20:34.040
Ah...

20:34.040 --> 20:36.630
I can see that you haven't had
any good romances until now.

20:36.630 --> 20:39.210
What? You can tell
just by seeing my hand?

20:39.510 --> 20:41.970
Also, you're rather purehearted, aren't you?

20:41.970 --> 20:46.100
And when you get stressed, you go
on shopping sprees. That's what your palm says.

20:46.640 --> 20:47.470
<i>Wow!</i>

20:47.930 --> 20:49.720
<i>This guy's the real deal!</i>

20:49.720 --> 20:50.350
So...

20:50.350 --> 20:50.980
Yes.

20:51.480 --> 20:55.020
Why do people confess
their feelings, was it?

20:55.020 --> 20:56.940
Yes.

20:56.940 --> 20:57.610
Wha...

20:58.110 --> 21:00.480
Why did you show up for our date
in your regular clothes?

21:00.480 --> 21:03.530
Huh? Doesn't everybody go on dates
wearing their own clothes?

21:03.740 --> 21:06.620
But President, you should be wearing your uniform
no matter what the time or occasion!

21:06.620 --> 21:08.910
That's why I thought
I'd coordinate with you!

21:09.290 --> 21:11.950
Why today of all days?

21:11.950 --> 21:13.910
Well, because...

21:14.210 --> 21:16.420
Because today is that kind of day.

21:19.550 --> 21:20.710
Let's go.

21:21.460 --> 21:22.760
All right.

21:24.300 --> 21:27.180
People start dating,
then break up without a thought.

21:27.640 --> 21:30.180
That person just might be your soul mate.

21:30.180 --> 21:35.190
You might go on loving that person forever,
even though he might not go on loving you.

21:36.060 --> 21:38.360
But if you love him,
you should stay with him.

21:38.360 --> 21:41.190
If you start hating him,
then all you have to do is leave, but...

21:51.830 --> 21:53.200
...doesn't it get all complicated...

21:53.700 --> 21:56.170
if you put it into words?

21:56.540 --> 21:58.710
You do have a point there.

21:59.170 --> 22:05.300
But it is a blessing to be able to love someone
so much that it turns your brain into mush.

22:05.300 --> 22:06.970
You should try it once.

22:09.890 --> 22:15.140
And it's only natural to want to be
in a relationship with the one you love.

22:16.230 --> 22:19.060
Freaking out that you might get dumped...

22:19.900 --> 22:22.190
Playing little games...

22:23.730 --> 22:28.110
You'll come up with all kinds of plans
and hold out for the perfect timing...

22:29.910 --> 22:33.990
But your heart will be pounding,
and nothing will make sense anymore.

22:36.540 --> 22:41.000
When it starts looking like the day will end
before you can say those words...

22:45.300 --> 22:47.010
I'm in love with you.

22:48.300 --> 22:51.010
Please be my boyfriend.

22:51.010 --> 22:54.010
You might find yourself blurting it out.

22:54.310 --> 22:58.730
<i>You fall in love, confess
and become a couple.</i>

22:58.730 --> 23:02.770
<i>Anyone would agree
that's a wonderful thing.</i>

23:02.770 --> 23:05.280
<i>But that notion is wrong.</i>

23:05.860 --> 23:09.990
<i>Love is only blissful until it's attained.</i>

23:10.410 --> 23:15.660
<i>After your feelings reach certain heights,
it's all downhill from there.</i>

23:15.660 --> 23:19.040
<i>That is what true love really is.</i>

23:19.040 --> 23:22.540
<i>Beyond love, there are no victors or losers.</i>

23:22.540 --> 23:25.000
<i>There's no telling if that person
is your soul mate or not.</i>

23:25.000 --> 23:27.630
<i>There might not even be eternal love.</i>

23:28.380 --> 23:29.300
Fine.

23:31.260 --> 23:32.050
<i>But...</i>

23:32.430 --> 23:35.890
<i>true love just might exist.</i>

23:35.890 --> 23:37.980
<i>One just needs to have a sharp mind.</i>

23:37.980 --> 23:41.730
<i>To seek true love, you must think.</i>

23:41.730 --> 23:43.560
<i>This is no easy task.</i>

23:43.560 --> 23:47.070
<i>Even so, it is only those
who continue to use their minds...</i>

23:48.990 --> 23:54.330
<i>who can be the first in the world
to attain true love.</i>
